(17654, 'GEOG', '205', 'Principles of Geomorphology', 'This course introduces underlying principles of geomorphology using examples from subfields of the discipline. Topics include the role of time and scale in geomorphic processes, as well as the role of water, hill-slope processes, soils, wind, and glaciation and ice in polar and alpine environs.', 0.50, NULL),
